  "rulesUnoIntro": "Each player is dealt 7 cards. Play a card of the same color or the same rank (number or matching action).",
  "rulesUnoPlay": "Skip — the next player loses a turn. Reverse with two players acts as Skip. +2 stacks only on +2, and +4 only on +4: the penalty adds up (two +2s make the next player draw 4). A +2 cannot be played on a +4. A player who does not stack draws the whole pile and is skipped. Two identical number cards (for example two yellow 8s) are discarded together: play one and the twin is thrown automatically. Action cards (+2, skip, reverse) and wilds are never dumped as a pair.",
  "rulesUnoWild": "A black card sets a new color. Play +4 only if you have no card of the current color. The next player may challenge: if the +4 was legal they draw 6; if not, the +4 player draws 4 and the challenger plays.",
  "rulesUnoDraw": "If you have no legal card, draw one from the deck. If it matches, you may play it now or keep it and pass. You cannot draw while you still have a legal play.",
  "rulesUnoWin": "Heads-up is first to 100 points; with 3+ players, first to 200. A round is won by emptying your hand.",
  "rulesUnoCall": "When you have one card left, tap “Uno!” immediately. Opponents can catch you for forgetting Uno only after one second — then you draw 2 cards.",
  "rulesUnoScoring": "The first to empty their hand wins the round and scores opponents’ cards: numbers at face value, actions 20, black cards 50. Heads-up is first to 100; with 3+ players, first to 200.",
